==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|finna}}, from {{inh|sv|non|finna}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*finþaną}}, from {{der|sv|ine-pro|*pent-||to go, pass; path, bridge}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/ˈfɪnːa/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-finna.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-irr|finner|fann|funnit|finn}}

# {{lb|sv|slightly|_|formal}} to [[find]], to locate, to discover
#: {{ux|sv|Var kan man '''finna''' en kopp kaffe här i närheten?|Where can you '''find''' a cup of coffee near here?}}
# {{lb|sv|formal}} to [[find]] (something to be a particular way)
#: {{ux|sv|Jag '''finner''' det mycket märkligt att ingen kan ta på sig ansvaret för det inträffade!|I '''find''' it very strange that nobody is willing to take responsibility for what has happened!}}
# {{lb|sv|passive|_|only}} to [[exist]]
#: {{ux|sv|Det '''finns''' nå'nstans en blå planet|There '''exists''' somewhere, a blue planet}}
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to [[find oneself]] (in a particular situation)
#: {{ux|sv|Han såg sig i spegeln och '''fann sig''' vara en mås|He looked in the mirror and '''found himself''' to be a gull}}
# {{lb|sv|reflexive|in "finna sig i"}} to [[put up with]]
#: {{ux|sv|Jag tänker inte '''finna mig i''' det där!|I won't '''put up with''' that!}}
#: {{ux|sv|Jag var helt enkelt tvungen att '''finna mig i''' det|I simply had to '''put up with''' it}}
# {{lb|sv|reflexive}} to maintain or (quickly) regain one's [[composure]] (particularly of having a good reply)
#: {{ux|sv|Åklagaren trodde han satt dit henne, men hon '''fann sig''' snabbt och gav ett övertygande svar|The prosecutor thought he had her, but she quickly '''regained her composure''' and gave a convincing answer}}

